; Integer division by zero must NOT return a value on any backend. All three
; abort with empty stdout and a nonzero exit: the EIR VM raises a
; "division by zero" runtime error (the oracle), the interpreter raises the
; same, and wasm's i64.div_s traps. The diagnostic strings differ (a trap is
; not the VM's message), but the conformance contract only compares stdout +
; success/failure class, and on that all three agree — so no expect-fail.
[fn main []
  [println [/ 1 0]]]
